{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Humanism in AI.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Humanism in AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"humanism in ai humanism in ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Humanism in AI.md","fileName":"Humanism in AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Humanism in AI","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Futures and Human Identity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Posthumanism","Anthropocentrism in AI Ethics","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Humanism in AI.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Humanism in AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"humanism in ai humanism in ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Humanism in AI.md","fileName":"Humanism in AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Humanism in AI","heading":"Humanism in AI","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Humanism in AI places human reason, dignity, freedom, or flourishing at the center of judgments about intelligent technology. It rejects the idea that technical capability or efficiency should determine its own goals and insists that machines should serve human purposes.\n\nThe position protects people from being subordinated to automated systems, but it can treat a historically specific picture of the human as universal. It may also neglect nonhuman life and environmental interests. [[Posthumanism]] and [[Anthropocentrism in AI Ethics]] expose these limits without eliminating the practical need to defend people against concentrated technological power.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Posthumanism","Anthropocentrism in AI Ethics","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Humanism in AI.md::2","so